# Multiple-Choice Quiz App

## Overview
This project is a Multiple-Choice Quiz App built using HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, and JavaScript. It allows users to answer a series of multiple-choice questions, calculates their score, and provides feedback on their performance.

## Features
- A set of 5-10 multiple-choice questions.
- Users can select one answer per question.
- Final score is displayed after the last question.
- Optionally shows correct answers after submitting.
- Scores are stored in localStorage for future reference.
- Includes a "Try Again" button to retake the quiz.

## Project Structure
```
quiz-app
├── src
│   ├── index.html        # Main HTML document for the quiz app
│   ├── css
│   │   └── styles.css    # Custom styles for the quiz app
│   ├── js
│   │   └── script.js      # JavaScript logic for the quiz app
│   └── data
│       └── questions.js   # Array of question objects
└── README.md             # Documentation for the project
```

## Getting Started
1. Clone the repository to your local machine.
2. Open the `src/index.html` file in your web browser to run the quiz app.
3. Follow the on-screen instructions to complete the quiz.

## Technologies Used
- HTML
- CSS
- Bootstrap
- JavaScript

## Notes
- Ensure you have a modern web browser for the best experience.
- Feel free to modify the questions in `src/data/questions.js` to customize the quiz.